  "_about": "After cauliflowermossgrape's Redline app (MIT), generated by design/gen_hud.py: G20-style rev bar with shift lights, big gear, shift point with the cold-engine guard, and every upshift graded. The scale runs to the redline's thousand + 1000; shift point = redline - the Shift point setting. Lights and rpm on top, the bar and its scale across the window, then the gear with SHIFT under it, oil and coolant, and the shift point, last shift, grade and cold note bottom right. Fitted (Nov 9 2026) to the HUD as BMW's own height-adjust frame shows it, x 120..680, y 100..380, and kept clear of the bottom-left x 120..350, y 235..380, where BMW draws its speed and speed-limit sign (and in Sport its rev band) over ours. To change it, copy this file into the app data folder layouts/ (scripts/deploy.sh); the app reloads it by itself. Widget types and tokens: see the header of hud.js.",
